(Architecture Guidelines and Performance Metrics. The chunking algorithm splits text into segments of approximately 500 tokens with a 50-token overlap. This window guarantees semantic continuity between adjacent chunks. When a user asks a question, the top 4 most relevant chunks are retrieved from ChromaDB. The system strictly instructs Gemini 1.5 Flash to ground its responses exclusively in the retrieved chunks. If a question cannot be answered from the provided chunks, the chatbot will decline rather than hallucinate.) Tj
ET
endstream
